Overview :  

3-tier application :
 [ Presentation Tier ]     <-- User Interface (Browser / Mobile App)
            │
            ▼
     [ Application Tier ]     <-- Brains & Logic (API / Middleware Server)
            │
            ▼
        [ Data Tier ]         <-- Database & Storage (SQL / NoSQL)
1. Presentation Tier (The Front End)
The presentation tier is the user interface and communication layer of the application. It is the part that users interact with directly on their devices.
• Function: Gathers inputs from the user, forwards requests to the application layer, and displays visual information back to the user.
• Technologies: HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, React, Angular, iOS/Android mobile apps.
• Example: The product display grid and "Add to Cart" button on an e-commerce platform
2. 2. Application Tier (The Logic / Middle Layer)
The application tier acts as the engine or "brain" of the software system. It sits between the frontend interface and the database backend, processing commands and making logical decisions.
• Function: Executes business logic, routes workflows, performs calculations, evaluates algorithms, and directly dictates how data is queried or updated.
• Technologies: Java, Node.js, Python, C#, PHP.
• Example: Checking if an item is in stock, verifying user authentication credentials, or processing credit card payments
3. Data Tier (The Back End)
The data tier is the dedicated home where all real-time and structural information resides.
• Function: Stores, retrieves, aggregates, and manages persistent application data while maintaining structural data integrity.
• Technologies: Relational databases like MySQL or PostgreSQL, NoSQL options like MongoDB, or object stores.
• Example: The database storing inventory levels, financial transaction receipts, and customer account profiles




 
